 "youtube": {
  "title": "Bubble Wrap History: It Was Meant to Be Wallpaper!",
  "description": "Bubble wrap history starts with a flop: it was invented as textured wallpaper, and nobody wanted it. So how did it end up in every package?\n\nIn 1957, engineers Alfred Fielding and Marc Chavannes sealed two shower curtains together in Hawthorne, New Jersey, and trapped air bubbles inside. The wallpaper idea failed, and greenhouse insulation didn't catch on either. Then IBM needed a safe way to ship its new 1401 computer, and the invention of bubble wrap finally found its real job: packaging.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a strange true story every day. What everyday thing do you think started as something else? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #bubblewrap #inventionhistory #stickstory",
